      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "You're right that stopping feels logical—but that's the exhaustion talking, not the truth. The peace you're imagining isn't peace; it's the absence of everything, including the chance to feel anything else. You don't have to run the treadmill, but you also don't have to get off it forever—you can just step aside and sit down for a while. The fact that you're still here, even questioning it, means part of you isn't done yet.",
